<title>HONG KONG: HK July retail sales up 7.0 pct in value on yr.</title>
<headline>HK July retail sales up 7.0 pct in value on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong July retail sales totalled a provisional HK$18.9 billion, up 7.0 percent on the year and up 8.0 percent on the month, Census and Statistics Department figures showed.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the value and volume of all retail outlets</p>
<p>						     July    June</p>
<p> Total retail sales (on-year)  - value   +7	+6</p>
<p>					 - volume  +3	+1</p>
<p>			  (on-month) - value   +8	-2</p>
<p>					 - volume  +9	-2</p>
<p>Breakdown by category (on-year)</p>
<p> Clothing and footwear	   - value   +5	+9</p>
<p>					 - volume  -1	+2</p>
<p>Jewellery, watches</p>
<p> clocks, valuable gifts	  - value   +5	+1</p>
<p>					 - volume  +4	-2</p>
<p>Consumer durables,</p>
<p> excluding cars		    - value   +10     +4</p>
<p>					 - volume  +9	+3</p>
<p> Department stores		 - value   +2	+12</p>
<p>					 - volume  -3	+7</p>
<p> Supermarkets			- value   +7	+9</p>
<p>					 - volume  +1	+3</p>
<p> Fuels				 - value   _9	-6</p>
<p>					 - volume  -16     -13</p>
<p> Motor vehicles		    - value   +34     +3</p>
<p>					 - volume  +32     +3</p>
<p> Food, alcoholic drinks and</p>
<p> tobacco			     - value   +5	+6</p>
<p>					 - volume  **	+1</p>
<p>** = virtually unchanged</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong News Room (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
